meta {
  name: Create Follow Request
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.community.graph.createFollowRequest
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "subject": "{{targetDid}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const response = res.getBody();
  if (response.uri) {
    bru.setVar("followRequestUri", response.uri);
    bru.setVar("followRequestCid", response.cid);
  }
}

docs {
  # Create Follow Request
  
  Sends a follow request to a user with a private profile.
  
  ## Request Body
  - `subject` (string): DID of the user to follow
  
  ## Response
  Returns the created follow request record:
  - `uri`: AT URI of the follow request record
  - `cid`: Content ID of the record
  
  ## Behavior
  - Only works if the target profile is private
  - Prevents duplicate requests (one pending request per requester/subject pair)
  - Creates a record with status "pending"
  - If profile is public, this should fail (use normal follow instead)
  
  ## Test Scenario
  Part of "Follow Request Flow":
  1. Alice has a private profile
  2. Bob authenticates
  3. Bob sends follow request to Alice
  4. Verify request created with status "pending"
  5. Alice can now see Bob's request in her incoming requests
  
  **Environment Variables Required:**
  - `{{targetDid}}`: Set this to the DID of the private profile to follow
  
  **Note:** Follow request URI is automatically saved to `{{followRequestUri}}` for use in approval/denial.
}
